Subject: [PATCH 08524/11362] Add follow-up: check whole-process-crash recovery
 on the scored ARC agent

User question this session: does the live agent have checkpoint/recovery
for spurious process crashes, given the exp6199 kill investigation. Answer
found two real, working resilience layers (generator self-heal via
_ensure_server() on every call; LLM-tier-failure fallback to non-LLM search,
documented in the submission kernel's own comment) and one unchecked layer:
a crash of the scored agent's own Python process mid-episode, where no
E3AgentPolicy state checkpoint exists and the competition's own external
ARC-AGI-3-Agents framework's restart behavior is unread this session.

Adds a NEW 2026-08-08 entry to ops/known-issues.md CURRENT ACTIVE PRIORITIES
(above the existing 2026-08-07 entry) scoping the follow-up as
investigate-first: read the framework's crash/restart semantics before
building any speculative checkpoint mechanism. Also cross-references a
same-signature prior incident already on record (exp6091's llama-server
kills, RULING section below) as worth checking against this session's
same-signature exp6199 finding.

